## THE DISCRIMINATING TEST -- RESULT (cycle-probe 1 2 4 8 16, execute-only, quiet machine)
REFITTED hardened-child law: instructions = 3.027e7 + 1.989e7 x n
  cross-check: 3.027e7 + 1.989e7 x 219 = 4.386e9, against the independently measured
  4,386,739,693 from s1-acceptance's n=219 run. Two separate runs agree.
NEW MARGINAL 19.89e6, against the predictions written down beforehand:
  per-AND-word (57.0x)      predicted 15.56e6   -- OFF BY 27.9%.  REFUTED.
  per-machine-word (261.5x) predicted 20.33e6   -- off by 2.2%.
  "fixed term unchanged"    predicted 19.89e6   -- exact.
    ^ 🪤 DO NOT read the child's fixed term as having MOVED (3.147e7 -> 3.027e7, -3.8%). The old
      3.147e7 was DERIVED from a single n=219 point using an assumed marginal, so it was never a
      measurement. The fixed term is structural traversal, the child's circuit did not change, and
      the elephant's own fixed term held to -0.035% across the same release. The right reading is
      that the derived value was ~3.8% off and this five-point refit corrected it. Written this
      way round deliberately: otherwise someone later reads a moved fixed term into a circuit that
      never changed.
  per-response fixed cost                       -- REFUTED by arithmetic, before the run.
ACTUAL saving ratio: elephant 0.3479e9 / child 1.77e6 = 196.6x, against
  AND words 57.0x (off 3.45x) | fingerprint B 173.0x (off 1.13x) | machine words 261.5x (off 1.33x)
CONCLUSION: the saving is ON THE GATE PATH and scales with MACHINE WORDS, not AND messages.
  It lands between the fingerprint-byte and machine-word units, which is what you would expect
  of removed instrumentation having BOTH a per-operation and a per-storage-bit component -- the
  recorders had exactly that (per-gate Vec pushes plus an SSA wire-id bus touched per bit).
  The mechanism is NOT nailed to a single unit and I am not claiming it is.

